WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.168
-She stars
in the new movie "Jolt,"

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.770
available on
Prime Video tomorrow.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:08.441
Please welcome the one and only
Kate Beckinsale!

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:17.316
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.316 --> 00:00:20.119
I mean, come on.
Mwah! Mwah!

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:22.722
Kate Beckinsale!

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:26.125
Welcome.
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:27.526
Thank you for being here.

00:00:27.526 --> 00:00:29.428
And now we're going to face off

00:00:29.428 --> 00:00:32.998
in a game called "Box of Lies."

00:00:32.998 --> 00:00:38.771
-♪ Box of Lies, Box of Lies,
Box of Lies, Box of Lies ♪

00:00:38.771 --> 00:00:42.508
-Now, here's how it works.
We have nine mystery boxes

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:45.678
containing objects
no one has ever seen before.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:48.047
On your turn, you pick a box,
and take out the object

00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:49.382
and describe it
to your opponent.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.483
And then, they have to guess

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:52.619
if you're lying
or telling the truth.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:53.887
I'm not gonna
look at you because...

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:54.921
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:56.022
We're gonna play three rounds.

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:58.658
Kate, you pick the first box.
-Okay.

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.192
Any suggestions at all?

00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:05.331
[ Audience shouting ]

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:06.665
All right, five it is, then.

00:01:06.665 --> 00:01:08.200
I have not
played this game before.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.335
Okay.
-All right.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.104
-What do I do now?
-Now you open the box

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:13.672
and then put it off
to the side on this side.

00:01:13.672 --> 00:01:15.208
Yeah, and I won't
look or listen.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:16.509
I'll make noise.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:18.044
Quest, can you
give us some drums?

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:19.045
I don't want to hear anything.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:22.548
♪♪

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:24.350
All right, perfect.
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.085
-Well, what if
I don't know what it is?

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:27.987
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:30.589
-This could be part
of the lie or the truth.

00:01:30.589 --> 00:01:33.126
-I can smell it,
but I don't know what it is.

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:34.394
-Okay. So it has a scent.
That's a hint.

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:38.097
-Can I move over and smell it?
-Yeah, sure.

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:43.136
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:44.704
-Am I allowed to deconstruct it?

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.306
I genuinely
don't know what this is.

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:47.940
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.843
It might be an English thing
but I've never -- what is that?

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:52.245
Oh! I know what it is.

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:54.781
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:57.216
-All right.
-I'm sucking at this already.

00:01:57.216 --> 00:01:59.285
-No.
-Okay.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:02.322
It's a small
floral arrangement...

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:08.928
-Yeah.
-...containing some corn dogs.

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:09.963
-Okay.

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.598
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:17.370
Small floral arrangement
of corn dogs.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.305
That sounds actually
pretty good to me.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.907
That's very -- it's American.

00:02:21.907 --> 00:02:23.209
Corn dogs.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.944
I can't smell them from here.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:26.378
I feel like
I would smell a hot dog.

00:02:26.378 --> 00:02:28.647
-I mean, it could be a bluff.
You know what I mean?

00:02:28.647 --> 00:02:31.818
But maybe it doesn't --
-But it's not Box of Bluffs.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.052
It's not Box of Bluffs.
-It's Box of Lies.

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:34.553
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.553 --> 00:02:35.588
-Uh, wait.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:38.658
Small floral arrangement
of corn dogs.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:40.993
Kate Beckinsale,
would you lie to me?

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:45.998
I will say that it is a...

00:02:45.998 --> 00:02:47.967
I think it's the truth.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:51.337
-I think it is, but I've never
touched a corn dog before.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:52.871
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.

00:02:52.871 --> 00:02:54.474
All right, now,
hold on a second.

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:56.242
Oh!
-Yes!

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:57.309
I win!
-Is that what it is?

00:02:57.309 --> 00:02:58.577
[ Cheers and applause ]
[ Ding! ]

00:02:58.577 --> 00:03:02.214
-So I got it.

00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:05.084
You're smelling --
I see now, I get it, yes.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.819
So, I got that one.
You could put that away.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:09.122
-Smelled like a doughnut, so
I was thrown off for a second.

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:10.956
-That's definitely a corn dog.
Oh, yeah.

00:03:10.956 --> 00:03:12.125
-Okay, good.
-All right.

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:15.662
Which one should I pick?
[ Audience shouting ]

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.429
I fee like --
Kate, you can put that there

00:03:17.429 --> 00:03:19.331
now, if you want to.

00:03:19.331 --> 00:03:23.302
Someone was very adamant on 6.
-No!

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:26.105
-"No." Why?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.474
"No!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.511
[ Grunting ]

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:35.214
-So it's a light object.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.214 --> 00:03:37.850
-This is my acting.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:41.721
[ Humming "Baby Elephant Walk" ]

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:44.123
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:51.497
♪♪

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.299
Okay.
Okay.

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:55.133
It's interesting.
-Okay. What you got?

00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:57.836
-Well, it's another thing
that you could smell, as well.

00:03:57.836 --> 00:04:03.142
I can smell it already.
Um...

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:05.344
-You're cooking up a lie!
You're cooking up a lie!

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:07.213
I can see
you're cooking up a lie.

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:12.685
-You can tell already?
-I feel like you're wanting to.

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:15.922
-It's a
Nintendo Entertainment System

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:22.462
with a cartridge that's made out
of a grilled-cheese sandwich.

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:26.732
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.732 --> 00:04:28.834
It's not funny.
It's not funny.

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:31.003
It's not time
to laugh at everything.

00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:33.373
Sometimes things are serious
in life.

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:35.541
-I bet this is an item that
you would have in your house.

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.710
Like, you've come up with that
because you've seen that.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.246
-In my house? You think
I would have that in my house?

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:41.680
-Yeah.
-A Nintendo Entertainment --

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.582
with a grilled cheese with it?

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:47.887
-That seems so on brand for you.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:49.088
-It is on brand.

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:51.857
Am I telling the truth
or telling a lie?

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:54.459
♪♪

00:04:54.459 --> 00:04:57.429
-You're telling a lie.

00:04:57.429 --> 00:04:59.665
-I'm telling the truth.
-No!

00:04:59.665 --> 00:05:02.101
Oh, no!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:04.036
-Ah, thank you!
You guys are good!

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:07.006
The audience helped me out.
You guys are good.

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:08.207
They kind of
helped me with that.

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:09.809
I love that, yeah.

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:11.376
I don't know if I --
It's tough to lie to you.

00:05:11.376 --> 00:05:13.245
You know, I'm a big fan of you.

00:05:13.245 --> 00:05:14.279
All right, guys.
Which one?

00:05:14.279 --> 00:05:16.081
[ Audience shouting ]

00:05:16.081 --> 00:05:18.550
I'm hearing 2.
-No!

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:21.687
[ Audience shouting ]

00:05:21.687 --> 00:05:25.458
[ Grunting ]

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:35.802
♪♪

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:41.040
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.443
♪♪

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:48.180
[ Laughter continues ]

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:54.586
In my box
was something very sweet.

00:05:54.586 --> 00:05:58.457
It is...

00:05:58.457 --> 00:06:00.993
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:04.696
...little dolls...

00:06:04.696 --> 00:06:07.733
with Olympic medals...

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:11.670
made out of Frosted Mini Wheats.

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:16.309
Which may be American product.

00:06:16.309 --> 00:06:19.378
-Is it specifically a wheat?

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:21.647
[ Laughter ]

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:23.949
-I mean,
I could try it after this.

00:06:23.949 --> 00:06:25.951
I don't have an allergy,
but I do know

00:06:25.951 --> 00:06:27.419
a Frosted Mini Wheat
when I see it.

00:06:27.419 --> 00:06:29.088
-You do?
I of course don't.

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:31.457
-Yes.
Weetabix.

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:32.591
-Oh, got it.
Okay.

00:06:32.591 --> 00:06:35.194
-But an American version
and frosted on one side.

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:37.864
-Fancy.

00:06:37.864 --> 00:06:42.501
And then, you say...
gold medals, you say?

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:44.537
-No, all three.
Representing all three.

00:06:44.537 --> 00:06:46.038
-Oh, really?
-First, second, and third.

00:06:46.038 --> 00:06:47.606
-Okay.
And do they have different

00:06:47.606 --> 00:06:49.408
facial expressions
or all the same?

00:06:49.408 --> 00:06:51.243
-They're barely faces.
They're just...

00:06:51.243 --> 00:06:53.345
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, okay.

00:06:53.345 --> 00:06:55.248
-They look like
they should be something,

00:06:55.248 --> 00:06:57.750
but they're made out of wheat.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:59.418
Little squares of wheat.

00:06:59.418 --> 00:07:00.953
-Oh, the dolls
are made of wheat.

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:02.221
-Squares of wheat.
Yes.

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:04.589
-Wearing medals.
-Little tiny medals.

00:07:04.589 --> 00:07:07.359
-In a receptacle of any kind?
-They're on a podium.

00:07:07.359 --> 00:07:09.629
-A podium?
-An Olympic podium.

00:07:09.629 --> 00:07:10.696
[ Laughter ]

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:13.632
-They're not.
You're lying.

00:07:13.632 --> 00:07:15.734
-What?
-I think you're lying.

00:07:15.734 --> 00:07:17.302
I don't think there's
such a thing in the world

00:07:17.302 --> 00:07:18.937
as a Mini Wheat doll,
let alone --

00:07:18.937 --> 00:07:21.507
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:21.507 --> 00:07:22.774
-You are correct!
[ Ding! ]

00:07:22.774 --> 00:07:24.410
Oh, my God!
You are so good!

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:26.345
-That's me!

00:07:26.345 --> 00:07:28.414
♪♪

00:07:28.414 --> 00:07:30.450
-Do you now know Mini Wheats?
-I don't.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.084
I'm not great at American
breakfast cereal.

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:33.552
-Oh, my gosh.
Next time you come on,

00:07:33.552 --> 00:07:35.954
we have to get you
Frosted Mini Wheats.

00:07:35.954 --> 00:07:37.690
We have to try American cereal.
-There could be no going back.

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.391
-No, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:39.391 --> 00:07:41.126
-I'm gonna give the win
to Kate Beckinsale.

00:07:41.126 --> 00:07:42.194
Come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:42.194 --> 00:07:43.896
[ Bell dinging ]
The greatest.

